    21	#      squares are ordered by their touched diagonal interval and paired greedily by the
    22	#      smallest adjacent gap. Any leftover square is inert.
    23	#    - For a matched pair, every touched cell of both squares emits perpendicular diagonal
    24	#      rays. The ray length is the number of empty diagonal cells strictly between the two
    25	#      squares.
    26	#    - Example on one backslash segment:
    27	#      square A touches path indices [2,3], square B touches [7,8], so there are indices
    28	#      [4,5,6] between them. Seed task: each touched magenta cell would shoot to the border.
