    30	#      two cells inside one square. This combo instead first groups pixels into squares, then
    31	#      pairs A with B, then uses the block-to-block gap 3 as the ray length.
    32	#
    33	# b) Complexity calibration:
    34	#    - Only one trigger shape class is used for activation: 2x2 squares. That keeps the
    35	#      object-recognition burden small while still forcing component parsing.
    36	#    - Pair gaps are limited to 2..4 cells, producing a small repeated length vocabulary.
    37	#    - Each segment carries at most one matched pair or one lone square. This avoids the
    38	#      longest-diagonal color heuristic being hijacked by magenta and keeps pairing local.
